    <section>
      <h2 id="non-commercial-nature-of-the-project">6. Non-commercial nature of the project</h2>
      <p>AuroFlow Panel is maintained as an independent, non-professional software project. Access to the panel does not constitute the purchase of a managed virtual machine, hosting subscription or professional technical support service.</p>
      <p>The publisher does not sell or allocate GitHub runner capacity. Users operate the application through their own third-party accounts and remain subject to the contractual relationships established with those providers.</p>
      <p>The absence of a fee charged by the publisher does not mean that third-party services are necessarily free of charge.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="source-code-and-redistribution">7. Source code and redistribution</h2>
      <p>The panel and the virtual machine engine are maintained in separate public repositories. Each repository may have its own license, documentation and distribution conditions.</p>
      <p>Public availability of source code does not, by itself, grant unrestricted permission to reproduce, modify, sublicense or redistribute it.</p>
      <p>Any license applicable to the project's source code does not automatically extend to proprietary operating systems, third-party binaries, trademarks, firmware or other independently licensed components.</p>
      <p>Modified versions and independent deployments must not falsely imply endorsement by the original publisher.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="external-services-and-links">8. External services and links</h2>
      <p>The website contains links to external websites, documentation, repositories and service providers.</p>
      <p>These external resources are operated independently of the publisher. Their content, availability, security and contractual conditions may change without notice.</p>
      <p>Users should consult the applicable terms and privacy policies before creating accounts, submitting credentials or transferring information to external services.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="reporting-unlawful-content">9. Reporting unlawful content</h2>
      <p>Requests concerning allegedly unlawful content, intellectual property infringement or other legal concerns may be submitted to contact@fox3000foxy.com.</p>
      <p>Reports should identify the relevant URL or repository, describe the disputed material, explain the basis of the complaint and provide sufficient information to allow the publisher to assess the request.</p>
      <p>Sensitive information and access credentials must not be included in public GitHub issues.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="maintenance-and-discontinuation">10. Maintenance and discontinuation</h2>
      <p>The publisher may modify, suspend, archive or discontinue the project, its documentation or its hosted authentication relay.</p>
      <p>No commitment is made to maintain compatibility with particular versions of external APIs, operating systems or infrastructure.</p>
      <p>Users are encouraged to retain independent copies of important data and configuration information rather than relying exclusively on the continued availability of the hosted panel.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="applicable-law">11. Applicable law</h2>
      <p>The project is operated from France. Matters concerning the publisher are subject to applicable French and European law, without prejudice to mandatory protections available to users in other jurisdictions.</p>
      <p>Any dispute shall be handled by the courts or authorities having jurisdiction under applicable law.</p>
      <p>Nothing in this notice limits statutory rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be waived.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 id="allocation-of-responsibilities">Allocation of responsibilities and third-party dependencies</h2>
      <p>
        AuroFlow Panel acts as a technical interface between the end user and independently operated third-party services.
      </p>
      <p>
        The publisher does not control the internal infrastructure, operational decisions, billing practices, retention policies or contractual restrictions of these providers.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users are responsible for reviewing the applicable terms, privacy policies, licensing requirements and usage restrictions before using any integrated service.
      </p>
      <p>
        The publisher provides information and warnings concerning known technical limitations, security risks and third-party dependencies. Such information does not constitute a certification, guarantee of compliance or authorization to use external resources.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users remain responsible for their accounts, credentials, workloads, virtual machine contents, resource consumption and configuration decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The publisher remains responsible for its own processing activities, distribution practices and obligations under applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in this provision excludes or transfers responsibilities that cannot lawfully be excluded or transferred.
      </p>
